        {
          "panel": 1,
          "shot": "Extreme Wide Shot",
          "visual": "Morning. Water City Tokyo, 2065. Canals weave between buildings where roads once were. Dismantled highway overpasses have been reclaimed by green vines. Light-networks pulse gently through the city's architecture like veins. A water-bus glides along a wide canal. Cherry blossom petals drift on the water's surface. Spring.",
          "environment": "env:water-city-tokyo-2065",
          "characters": [],
          "dialogue": [
            {
              "speaker": "Narration",
              "text": "The canals are blue this morning.",
              "ja": "今朝も、運河は青い。"
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Narration",
              "text": "Tokyo rebuilt itself around water. When the sea levels rose, they didn't fight it. They let the city become something new.",
              "ja": "東京は、水とともに生まれ変わった。海面が上がった時、人々は抗わなかった。街を、新しいものにした。"
            }
          ],
